Alchemy @VERSION@ (unofficial build)
====================================

Alchemy is a free-hand generative drawing environment: you sketch a shape and
attach "affect" modules that reproduce, recolour, mirror or animate it.

Source and provenance
---------------------
  Original project : "Alchemy" by Karl D.D. Willis
                     https://karldd.github.io/alchemy
  Source of this
  build            : https://github.com/pbiswal/Alchemy  commit @COMMIT@
  Upstream tree    : the unmaintained upstream (last release: Alchemy 008, 2010;
                     last commit: 2018-10-30)

This is an unofficial community build. It is not published, endorsed or reviewed
by the original author. Modifications are distributed under the same GPLv3 terms
as the original work.

Requirements
------------
  Java 17 or newer (this build line is tested on JDK 17, 21 and 25).
  Start with ./Alchemy (Linux/macOS), Alchemy.bat (Windows), or by double
  clicking alchemy.jar. JAVA_HOME is honoured when set; set ALCHEMY_OPTS for
  extra JVM options.

Platform status
---------------
  Linux x86_64 : starts, all 28 module archives register (verified in CI).
  Windows x64  : starts, all 28 module archives register (verified in CI).
  macOS        : starts and the window opens, but the bundled 2018 Quaqua
                 look-and-feel and the com.apple.eawt glue throw during
                 start-up. Treated as best-effort; see MAINTENANCE.md.
  Pen / tablet : JPen native libraries for Linux x86 (32/64), Windows (32/64) and
                 Intel macOS are bundled in lib/jpen. Apple Silicon builds are
                 not bundled; a keyboard and mouse still works.
  Demo shapes  : the "shapes/" folder shipped with Alchemy 008 was never
                 committed to the repository, so it is not in this archive.

